# Skill Hub local-development template.
# Copy with `task env:init` (or `go -C tools/devctl run . env-init`).
# Values below are local-only placeholders. Keep every secret blank until its
# profile is intentionally enabled; never commit the resulting .env file.

# Core profile: platform and local infrastructure
DATABASE_URL=postgres://skillhub:skillhub@localhost:5432/skillhub?sslmode=disable
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
DEV_CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
COOKIE_INSECURE=1
DEV_LOGIN=1
OPERATOR_USER_IDS=
BETA_ALLOWLIST=
IMPORT_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
IMPORT_EXTRA_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1
OBJSTORE_ENDPOINT=localhost:8333
OBJSTORE_ACCESS_KEY=skillhubdev
OBJSTORE_SECRET_KEY=skillhubdevsecret
OBJSTORE_BUCKET=skillhub
OBJSTORE_SSL=0
LLM_SERVICE_URL=
# Required whenever LLM_SERVICE_URL is set. Shared only by the Go control plane
# and the internal Python LLM service; never expose it to sandbox workloads.
LLM_SERVICE_TOKEN=
METRICS_ADDR=
# The three retention windows below were ratified 2026-08-23 (PDM-006 / 05 R-1a).
# Go duration strings. All three are still fail-closed with no code default: an
# unset value must keep meaning "nobody set a policy", not "use the last number
# someone wrote in an example file".
#
# Download artifact: 30 天. Revised the same day from 一週 (168h), which was
# shorter than the 14-day closed beta it has to survive — a participant who
# packaged on day 2 would find it gone on day 9, mid-study, and the funnel's
# last segment measures exactly that download. NFR-002a rule 1 now states the
# floor: download retention >= the current observation window. 720h also lines
# it up with PDM-006's 30-day Run Artifact window.
DOWNLOAD_ARTIFACT_RETENTION=720h
# Product analytics events: 一年. Ratified LONGER than ADR-029 決策 5's proposed
# 180 days. That ADR argued 180 covers one beta plus one scope review and that
# audit's 400 days was unnecessary; 365 is close to the number it rejected, and
# this is the one data class users produce without submitting anything
# (02:O11Y-004), so the consent disclosure carries 365, not 180.
ANALYTICS_RETENTION=8760h
# Trace event retention. 3 個月 — matches PDM-006's proposal exactly. Required by
# `maintenance rotate-partitions`, which refuses to run without it.
TRACE_RETENTION=2160h
# PDM-010 free run allowance. IMPORTANT: unset does NOT mean "off" — unset
# enforces the proposed numbers (20 first window / 30 per window / 5 per day),
# because an unset allowance would leave the platform's only real cost ceiling
# open. `off` is the explicit escape hatch and it disables the display too, so
# no screen claims an allowance nobody enforces (04 乙-2).
# Turned off 2026-08-23 for the closed beta — ADR-055. Per-run brakes are
# unaffected: the gateway key still carries max_budget $0.50 and SBX-013 still
# caps 300K in / 60K out per run. What is uncapped is the NUMBER of runs.
RUN_QUOTA=off

# M5 generation allowance (GEN-004, ADR-047 決策 5). Same asymmetry as RUN_QUOTA:
# unset enforces the proposed numbers (20 first window / 30 per window / 10 per
# day), `off` is the explicit escape hatch and disables the display with it.
# A SECOND variable on purpose — one switch for both allowances would be the
# shared pool ADR-047 決策 5 ruled against, and a generation would quietly eat a
# trial run's balance.
# Turned off 2026-08-23 alongside RUN_QUOTA (ADR-056).
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TURNING GENERATE_SKILL_EXPOSED ON. The sentence that used to
# be here — "the gateway key still carries max_budget" — was true of runs and
# FALSE of generation, and the difference is the whole risk. A run mints a fresh
# virtual key with its own max_budget per attempt (SBX-008). A generation goes
# through the shared static LITELLM_API_KEY, whose max_budget is a cumulative
# deployment-wide balance — so draining it does not merely stop generation, it
# stops /embed, index-time enrichment and every LLM judge with it.
#
# What actually bounds one generation: a 4000-character description in and a
# 16000-token ceiling out, ~$0.0055 with the default mini model. What bounds the
# NUMBER of them, with this off: one in flight per workspace (an in-process gate
# in skill/admission) and nothing else. There is no rate limit anywhere in the
# platform yet — NFR-001 clause 5 asks for one, and 04 丙-54 tracks it.
GENERATE_QUOTA=off

# ADR-052's hard boundary between 開工 and 曝光. `on` mounts POST /skills/generate
# and makes GET /me list `generate_skill`; anything else (including unset) means
# the route does not exist and the web never draws the entry point.
#
# The asymmetry runs the OTHER way from the two allowances above, deliberately:
# an allowance left unconfigured leaves the cost ceiling open, so unset must mean
# enforced; an entry point left unconfigured simply is not there yet.
#
# Do not turn this on until 01 §11.2's first funnel segment has a reading. A beta
# participant who meets "搜不到 → 生成一個" is no longer measuring whether search
# works, and that number has one chance with twelve people.
GENERATE_SKILL_EXPOSED=

# GitHub OAuth is optional when DEV_LOGIN=1. Keep production credentials blank.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=

# Model profile: required only for LiteLLM-backed operations.
# Provider credentials belong to the LiteLLM process only (ADR-017).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
LITELLM_API_KEY=

# Run and sandbox profile: opt-in and potentially paid.
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_PROVIDERS=
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=
SKILLHUB_SANDBOX_NETWORK=
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:4000
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:4000
SKILLHUB_MODEL_GATEWAY_KEY=
SKILLHUB_RUN_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
SKILLHUB_RUN_MAX_BUDGET_USD=0.50
SKILLHUB_RUN_TPM_LIMIT=200000
SKILLHUB_TRACE_INGEST_URL=http://localhost:8080
SKILLHUB_TRACE_INGEST_SECRET=

# Tests: intentionally blank so normal tests cannot spend money by accident.
# SKILLHUB_TEST_DATABASE_URL needs a separately created test database.
SKILLHUB_TEST_DATABASE_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_SANDBOX_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
SKILLHUB_E2E_GATEWAY_URL=
SKILLHUB_E2E_GATEWAY_KEY=
SKILLHUB_E2E_EGRESS_NETWORK=
SKILLHUB_E2E_RUNTIME_IMAGE=
QA002_CORPUS=
